values ('d0e1f2a3-4b5c-4d18-9e78-8f9a0b1c2d08', 'metaphysics', 'Metaphysics', 'Students explain major metaphysical questions about existence, identity, modality, causation, time, objects, mind, and freedom; reconstruct and evaluate classic and contemporary arguments with precision and charity; compare realist, nominalist, reductionist, anti-reductionist, Humean, and non-Humean theories; use logical and modal vocabulary to clarify ontological commitments and possible-worlds reasoning; connect metaphysics to science, mind, social categories, religion, ethics, and ordinary life; and produce a polished research paper with a clear thesis, objections, replies, and source-based argument.');

